<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.15.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02005</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.15.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2cc89a6c-fe88-4466-85a6-e14111074785</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item><emphasis>Select three</emphasis> quadratic expressions written in vertex form.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>\(y=(x-2)^2 + 1\) </item>
  <item> \(y=x^2 - 4\) </item>
  <item> \(y=x(x+1)\) </item>
  <item> \(y=(x+3)(x+3)\) </item>
  <item> \(y=(x-4)^2 + 6\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(y=(x-2)^2 + 1\), \(y=x^2 - 4\), \(y=(x-4)^2 + 6\)</para>
<para>Examine the following two equations and use them to answer questions 2 – 5. One defines function \(m\) and the other defines function \(p\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(m(x)=x(x+6)\) </item>
  <item> \(p(x)=(x+3)^2−9\) </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>How do you know that the expressions defining \(m\) and \(p\) are equivalent?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Both expressions are equal to \(x^2+6x\). </item>
  <item> Both expressions are equal to \(x^2-6x\). </item>
  <item> Both expressions are equal to \(2x+6\). </item>
  <item> Both expressions are equal to \(x^2-3\). </item>
</list>
<emphasis> </emphasis>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Both expressions are equal to \(x^2+6x\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Recall \(m(x)=x(x+6)\) and \(p(x)=(x+3)^2−9\). What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph of \(m\)? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -3</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>Recall \(m(x)=x(x+6)\) and \(p(x)=(x+3)^2−9\). What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph of \(m\)? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -9</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Recall \(m(x)=x(x+6)\) and \(p(x)=(x+3)^2−9\). What are the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph of \(p\)? </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>\((0,0)\) and \((-6,0)\) </item>
  <item> \((0,0)\) and \((6,0)\) </item>
  <item> \((0,0)\) and \((0,-6)\) </item>
  <item> \((0,0)\) and \((0,6)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((0,0)\) and \((-6,0)\). The graphs of \(m\) and \(p\) are the same. The zeros of \(m\) are 0 and -6, which give the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph.</para>
<para>For questions 6 – 11, enter the coordinates of the vertex of the graph that represents the equation.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Find the coordinates of the vertex for the equation \(y=(x-3)^2 + 5\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 3</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 5</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>Find the coordinates of the vertex for the equation \(y=(x+7)^2 + 3\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -7</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 3</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>Find the coordinates of the vertex for the equation \(y=(x-4)^2\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<emphasis> </emphasis>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 4</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 0</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>Find the coordinates of the vertex for the equation \(y=x^2 - 1\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 0</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Find the coordinates of the vertex for the equation \(y=2(x+1)^2-5\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -5</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="11" type="enumerated">
  <item>Find the coordinates of the vertex for the equation \(y=-2(x+1)^2-5\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>-1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -5</para>
<para>For questions 12 – 14, answer the questions about the \(x\)- and \(y\)-coordinates of the vertex, and whether the function opens up or down.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="12" type="enumerated">
  <item>For function \(f(x)=(x-4)^2-5\), find the coordinates of the vertex and determine if the function opens up or down.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 4</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -5</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> For the function \(f(x)=(x-4)^2-5\), does the graph open up or down? </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Up </item>
  <item> Down </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> The graph opens upward. The squared term has a positive coefficient (1).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="13" type="enumerated">
  <item>For function \(g(x)=-x^2+5\), find the coordinates of the vertex and determine if the function opens up or down.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<emphasis> </emphasis>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>0</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 5</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> For the function \(g(x)=-x^2+5\), does the graph open up or down? </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Up </item>
  <item> Down </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> The graph opens downward. The squared term has a negative coefficient (-1).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="14" type="enumerated">
  <item>For function \(h(x)=2(x+1)^2-4\), find the coordinates of the vertex and determine if the function opens up or down.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -4</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> For the function \(h(x)=2(x+1)^2-4\), does the graph open up or down? </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Up </item>
  <item> Down </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> The graph opens upward. The squared term has a positive coefficient (2).</para></section>
</content>
